From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python: Build the testing module with NOSTRIP

holoscan.testing._testing is the only installed nanobind module built
without NOSTRIP, so nanobind links it with -Wl,-s. A distribution that
splits debug symbols out of what it installs then finds it already
stripped, and gets no debug information for it.

Build it with NOSTRIP, as holoscan._core and the module bindings are.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
diff --git a/python/holoscan/testing/CMakeLists.txt b/python/holoscan/testing/CMakeLists.txt
index f988b8825..9152df55e 100644
--- a/python/holoscan/testing/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/python/holoscan/testing/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 
-nanobind_add_module(holoscan_testing_python STABLE_ABI harness.cpp adapters.cpp registered_adapters.cpp)
+nanobind_add_module(holoscan_testing_python STABLE_ABI NOSTRIP harness.cpp adapters.cpp registered_adapters.cpp)
 target_link_libraries(holoscan_testing_python PRIVATE holoscan::testing holoscan::params)
 target_include_directories(holoscan_testing_python PRIVATE
     "${HOLOSCAN_PYTHON_BINDING_SERVICES_INCLUDE_DIR}")
